{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]I woke up this morning, had a note upon my door
[C]Don’t make me no coffee babe, I won’t be back no more
[C]That’s all she wrote (Dear John)
[G]I’ve sent your saddle [C]home
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Jonah got along in the belly of the whale Daniel in the lions den,
I know a guy that didn’t get a long and he won’t get a chance again
That’s all she wrote (Dear John)
I’ve sent your saddle home
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Didn’t forward no address, she didn’t say goodbye
She just said if you get blue, just hang your head and cry
That’s all she wrote (Dear John)
I’ve sent your saddle home
{end_of_verse}

